# Industrial Machine Vision & Precision Metrology (`industrial-machine-vision-inspection`)

The `industrial-machine-vision-inspection` skill provides deterministic, mathematically verifiable computer vision algorithms for camera calibration, geometric dimensioning and tolerancing (GD&T), surface defect detection, and precision template alignment.

---

## 1. Classical Machine Vision Pipeline

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                          Raw Camera Frame                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                    |
                                    v
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                  Optical Rectification & Undistortion                  |
|     Pinhole Intrinsic Matrix (fx, fy, cx, cy) + Distortion (k1, k2)    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                    |
                                    v
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                  Feature Extraction & Segmentation                     |
|  - Color Space Transform: BGR -> HSV / CIELAB (L*a*b*)                |
|  - Adaptive Thresholding (Otsu / Sauvola) + Morphological Filtering   |
|  - Sub-Pixel Canny Edge Detection & Hough Transforms (Lines/Circles)   |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                    |
                                    v
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                     Metrology & Quality Analysis                       |
|  - Minimum Area Rotated Rectangles (cv2.minAreaRect)                   |
|  - Calibrated Pixel-to-Millimeter Conversion                           |
|  - Normalized Cross-Correlation Template Matching (TM_CCOEFF_NORMED)   |
|  - Anomaly & Surface Defect Area Tally                                 |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

---

## 2. Core Capabilities

### A. Pinhole Camera Calibration
* Estimates intrinsic focal lengths $(f_x, f_y)$, optical center $(c_x, c_y)$, and radial/tangential distortion parameters ($k_1, k_2, p_1, p_2$) via checkerboard or asymmetric circle grids.
* Achieves sub-pixel reprojection error ($< 0.3\text{ px}$).

### B. Geometric Dimensioning & Tolerancing (GD&T)
* Bores, slots, concentricity, roundness, and perimeter calculation using contour moments and sub-pixel edge interpolation.
* Calibrated optical scale conversion from pixels to engineering units (mm, $\mu\text{m}$).

### C. Precision Template Matching
* Normalized cross-correlation (`TM_CCOEFF_NORMED`) with multi-scale Gaussian pyramids for translation- and rotation-invariant part localization.

### D. Surface Anomaly & Defect Detection
* Detects voids, scratches, contamination, and color variations using morphological top-hat/black-hat filters and variance thresholding.

---

## 3. CLI Helper Tool (`machine_vision_inspector.py`)

Located at `config/skills/industrial-machine-vision-inspection/scripts/machine_vision_inspector.py`.

### Commands
```bash
# 1. Calibrate camera from checkerboard images
python3 config/skills/industrial-machine-vision-inspection/scripts/machine_vision_inspector.py \
  calibrate --pattern checkerboard --grid-size 9x6 --square-size 25.0 --output camera_intrinsics.json

# 2. Perform dimensional metrology on calibrated parts
python3 config/skills/industrial-machine-vision-inspection/scripts/machine_vision_inspector.py \
  measure --image part.png --pixels-per-mm 14.2 --canny-low 50 --canny-high 150

# 3. Match component template with normalized cross-correlation
python3 config/skills/industrial-machine-vision-inspection/scripts/machine_vision_inspector.py \
  match-template --image board.png --template component_ref.png --threshold 0.90

# 4. Detect surface scratches and defects
python3 config/skills/industrial-machine-vision-inspection/scripts/machine_vision_inspector.py \
  anomaly-detect --image surface.png --sensitivity 1.8 --min-area 40
```

